# Foundry tenancy

Use one Azure AI Foundry project for every tenant. That project is the shared model and agent runtime. The project does not isolate client companies. The .NET API isolates them.

- Keep this single Foundry project for the demo and for the first clients.
- Verify the short-lived signed token on every request, and use only that tenant’s prompt and tools.
- Keep conversation history in the application store, partitioned by tenant.
- Keep client API secrets in Key Vault, partitioned by tenant.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD: caller picks a Foundry project or a tenant
var project = req.Body.FoundryProject;

// ✅ GOOD: one Foundry project; the verified token selects the tenant
var tenant = await VerifyToken(req.Headers.Authorization);
var prompt = await store.GetPrompt(tenant.TenantId);
var secret = await keyVault.GetClientSecret(tenant.TenantId);
```

Keep enforcing the security, privacy, compliance, and accessibility rules. This rule fixes the Foundry project boundary.
